WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.960
House of the Dragon is a Game&nbsp;
of Thrones prequel show that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:09.280
confirmed by HBO’s president to air in 2022.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.320
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet&nbsp;
unfinished Fire And Blood volume 2 book.&nbsp;

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:20.000
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the legendary&nbsp;
Aegon the Conqueror, creator of the Iron Throne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.520
and goes on to recount the generations of&nbsp;
Targaryens who fought to hold that iconic seat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.440
all the way up to the civil war that&nbsp;
nearly tore their dynasty apart.”&nbsp;

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.760
That's Fire And Blood volume 1. The&nbsp;
yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:39.600
will continue from where part 1 ended, with&nbsp;
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.560
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with&nbsp;
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:50.400
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:56.080
showrunners and executive producers. George R.&nbsp;
R. Martin will also serve as executive producer.&nbsp;

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:00.960
The key event of the prequel will be the&nbsp;
Dance of the Dragon, a Targaryen civil war.&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.760
Although it's a Targaryen civil war, Targaryens&nbsp;
are not the only key characters from this time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:11.520
period, one major character among them being&nbsp;
Corlys Velaryon, known as the Sea Snake.&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.000
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating&nbsp;
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.&nbsp;

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.000
A war of succession between Aegon&nbsp;
II and his half-sister Rhaenyra over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.000
their father Viserys I's throne.
Both of them thought they belonged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.080
on the Iron Throne. When people started&nbsp;
declaring for one of them or the other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.960
their fight divided the kingdoms in two
As I already said, Game of Thrones prequel series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:38.640
House of the Dragon, though based on the George&nbsp;
RR Martin's Targaryen history book Fire &amp; Blood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.880
will not feature Targaryens only&nbsp;
but many other houses and many other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:49.360
legendary figures from that time period as well,
including the Velaryons had for centuries remained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:55.040
the oldest and closest allies of the Targaryens.
The sea was their element, not the sky.&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:01.280
During the Conquest, it was Velaryon ships that&nbsp;
carried Aegon’s soldiers across Blackwater Bay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.080
and later formed the greater&nbsp;
part of the royal fleet.&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.600
The most famous and strongest Velaryion to&nbsp;
ever live is also one of the main characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:15.120
in the upcoming House of the Dragon show&nbsp;
- Corlys Velaryon, known as the Sea Snake.&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.880
He is a fabled Lord of the Tides&nbsp;
during Targaryen civil war,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:25.600
Master of Driftmark, and head of House Velaryon.
House Velaryon, much like House Targaryen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.200
is of Valyrian descent, and&nbsp;
its members often have Valyrian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:35.440
features, such as silver hair, purple eyes.
He was the husband of Princess Rhaenys Targaryen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:41.360
the Queen-Who-Never-Was. During the Dance of&nbsp;
the Dragons, he became Hand to Queen Rhaenyra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:47.200
Targaryen who was his niece and daughter-in-law.
By the of age seven-and-thirty, Corlys was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:51.120
hailed as the greatest seafarer&nbsp;
the Seven Kingdoms had ever known.&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.840
Corlys was born in 53 AC to the&nbsp;
eldest son of Lord Daemon Velaryon.&nbsp;

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.320
He was named after his&nbsp;
great-great-uncle, Ser Corlys Velaryon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:05.120
who served King Aegon the Conqueror as the&nbsp;
first Lord Commander of the Kingsguard.&nbsp;

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:10.240
Ser Corlys sailed aboard his Sea Snake, a&nbsp;
ship he designed and built, on nine great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:17.280
voyages to Essos. During his final voyage on Sea&nbsp;
Snake, Corlys filled the ship's hold with gold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:22.480
and bought twenty more ships at Qarth,&nbsp;
loading them with spices, elephants, and silk.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.360
Only fourteen ships reached&nbsp;
Driftmark and all the elephants died,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.080
but it was still more than enough to make Corlys&nbsp;
become the wealthiest man in all of Westeros.&nbsp;

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.680
He took his nickname "Sea&nbsp;
Snake" from his famous ship.&nbsp;

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:42.400
Ser Corlys became head of House Velaryon and Lord&nbsp;
of the Tides after the death of his grandsire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:47.600
Richer than Lords Lannister or Hightower&nbsp;
through his expeditions, Lord Corlys used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:53.200
his great wealth to construct a new seat, High&nbsp;
Tide, where he stored his eastern treasures.&nbsp;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.840
In 90 AC, Corlys married the sixteen-year-old&nbsp;
Princess Rhaenys Targaryen, the only child of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.960
Prince Aemon Targaryen, who in turn was the&nbsp;
eldest son of King Jaehaerys I Targaryen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:12.240
Two years later, Corlys sailed his fleet to Tarth,&nbsp;
to aid Prince Aemon in fighting the Myrish exiles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:18.080
who had invaded the island. Shortly before they&nbsp;
left, Corlys's wife announced she was pregnant.&nbsp;

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:24.400
During the campaign, Prince Aemon died, leading&nbsp;
King Jaehaerys I Targaryen to appoint a new heir&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:30.160
to the throne. He chose his second son&nbsp;
Baelon over Aemon's only heir, Rhaenys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:36.640
thereby also passing over Corlys and Rhaenys's&nbsp;
unborn child. Furious over this decision, Corlys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:42.320
gave up his admiralty and his place on the king's&nbsp;
small council and returned to Driftmark with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:50.880
his wife. In late 92 AC, Rhaenys gave birth to a&nbsp;
daughter, Laena. A son, Laenor, followed in 94 AC.&nbsp;

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:58.720
When Prince Baelon died in 101 AC, King Jaehaerys&nbsp;
I's succession became unclear again, and reports&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.680
reached the court that Corlys was gathering&nbsp;
ships and men to defend the rights of his son.&nbsp;

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:09.360
When the king declared a Great Council would&nbsp;
be held at Harrenhal to settle the succession,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:13.280
Corlys and his wife traveled there,&nbsp;
using their wealth and influence to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:18.160
try and persuade the lords present to vote&nbsp;
for Laenor, after Rhaenys and Laena had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:24.640
passed over once again on account of their gender.
Corlys's fame, reputation, and wealth did much to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:29.840
support Laenor's claim, but in the end, Baelon's&nbsp;
son Viserys received the majority of the votes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.320
and was named Prince of Dragonstone.
Following the death of Queen Aemma Arryn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:41.760
in 105 AC, Grand Maester Runciter suggested to&nbsp;
King Viserys I Targaryen that he take Corlys's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:46.960
twelve-year-old daughter, Laena, to wife. King&nbsp;
Viserys, however, chose Alicent Hightower.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:52.480
Angered by the third time his wife and&nbsp;
children had been scorned by House Targaryen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.880
Corlys and his family did not&nbsp;
attend the wedding in 106 AC.&nbsp;

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:03.040
Instead, he made an alliance with Prince Daemon&nbsp;
Targaryen, King Viserys's younger brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:08.000
equally angered by the king's marriage.
Lord Corlys and his fleets fought alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:13.280
Prince Daemon Targaryen during the War for&nbsp;
the Stepstones. When Daemon declared himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:19.280
the King of the Stepstones and the Narrow Sea,&nbsp;
Corlys placed the crown on the new king's head.&nbsp;

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:25.840
In 113 AC, King Viserys I and his small council&nbsp;
began discussions concerning a betrothal for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:31.840
Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen, Viserys's heir.&nbsp;
They eventually agreed on Corlys's son, Laenor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:38.240
Laenor and Rhaenyra were married&nbsp;
in 114 AC and gave him 3 grandsons.&nbsp;

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:44.880
By 115 AC, Corlys saw his daughter Laena wed to&nbsp;
Daemon with his blessing. Through this marriage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:51.360
Corlys would have two more grandchildren: the twin&nbsp;
girls Baela and Rhaena Targaryen, born in 116 AC.&nbsp;

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:57.120
The children of Corlys and Princess&nbsp;
Rhaenys Targaryen both died in 120 AC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:02.720
Laena Velaryon from childbed fever and Ser Laenor&nbsp;
Velaryon from a quarrel with a knight which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:08.560
rumored to have been organized by Daemon. Later&nbsp;
in the same year Prince Daemon, Laena's widower,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:12.000
married Princess Rhaenyra&nbsp;
Targaryen, Laenor's widow.&nbsp;

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:17.360
Lord Corlys Velaryon sat on the black council&nbsp;
during the civil war known as the Dance of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:23.200
Dragons; he was the greatest lord to pledge his&nbsp;
strength to the cause of Queen Rhaenyra Targaryen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:29.440
who was opposed by her half-brother, King Aegon II&nbsp;
Targaryen. More than half of Rhaenyra's army was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:35.680
made up of men sworn to House Velaryon. Corlys's&nbsp;
fleets also gave the blacks superiority at sea.&nbsp;

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:42.080
When Lord Bartimos Celtigar urged the princess&nbsp;
to fly from Dragonstone to King’s Landing at once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:47.040
and reduce the city to ash and bone with&nbsp;
her dragon, Corlys demanded to know how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:52.160
that would serve them, telling him "we want&nbsp;
to rule the city, not burn it to the ground".&nbsp;

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.080
The Sea Snake commanded the Velaryon&nbsp;
fleet when it closed off the Gullet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:01.200
and sailed back and forth from Dragonstone and&nbsp;
Driftmark, blocking all shipping entering or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:06.400
leaving Blackwater Bay and thereby choking&nbsp;
off trade to and from King's Landing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:12.960
Eventually, the Velaryon blockade was broken by&nbsp;
the Battle in the Gullet and High Tide was sacked.&nbsp;

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.680
When his wife Rhaenys flew to Rook's&nbsp;
Rest to give aid to Lord Staunton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:24.400
who was besieged by the forces of Aegon II, she&nbsp;
fell in battle against King Aegon II and Sunfyre,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:30.880
and Prince Aemond Targaryen and Vhagar. When&nbsp;
news of Rhaenys's death reached Dragonstone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:36.960
Corlys blamed Rhaenyra for Rhaenys's death, as she&nbsp;
had forbidden her sons from accompanying Rhaenys.&nbsp;

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:43.680
In late 129 AC, Rhaenyra's son, Prince&nbsp;
Jacaerys brought the Lord of the Tides back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:49.280
into the fold by naming him Hand of the Queen.&nbsp;
Together the Hand and Jacaerys planned an assault&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:55.280
upon King’s Landing. Not long after, one of the&nbsp;
riderless dragons, Seasmoke, took onto his back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.280 --> 00:09:01.680
a fifteen-year-old boy known as Addam of Hull.
Lord Corlys went so far as to petition Queen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.320
Rhaenyra to remove the taint of bastardy&nbsp;
from Addam and his brother, Alyn.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:11.520
The queen complied and Addam Velaryon&nbsp;
became Corlys's heir to Driftmark.&nbsp;

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:15.920
After the queen took King's Landing, as&nbsp;
Lord Ormund Hightower's host advanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:20.480
slowly on King's Landing, with Prince&nbsp;
Daeron scouting ahead on his dragon,&nbsp;

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:24.400
Lord Corlys suggested to Rhaenyra&nbsp;
that the time had come to talk.&nbsp;

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:31.520
He urged the queen to offer pardons to Lord Borros&nbsp;
Baratheon, Ormund Hightower and House Lannister.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:37.120
He proposed to let the Faith of the Seven take&nbsp;
charge of Queen Alicent Hightower and Queen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:42.720
Helaena Targaryen, so that they might spend the&nbsp;
rest of their lives in prayer and contemplation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:47.280
Corlys suggested that Princess Jaehaera&nbsp;
Targaryen, the daughter of Rhaenyra's rival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:53.040
King Aegon II, be made his own ward,
and in due time married to Rhaenyra's son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:58.080
Prince Aegon the Younger, binding the two&nbsp;
halves of House Targaryen together once again.&nbsp;

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:04.000
Rhaenyra demanded to know what of her half&nbsp;
brothers, Aegon II, Aemond, and Daeron.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:10.320
Lord Corlys suggested they be spared and sent to&nbsp;
the Wall. When Corlys mentioned the sacred vows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:15.840
of the Night's Watch, Rhaenyra questioned the&nbsp;
vows of oathbreakers, stating that "Their vows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:21.840
did not trouble them when they took my throne."
Her husband, Prince Daemon, echoed the queen's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:26.880
misgiving and suggested a hard line, but&nbsp;
the queen decided to steer a middle course.&nbsp;

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:32.720
After the Two Betrayers switched sides, Lord&nbsp;
Corlys was the only person on the black council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:39.120
to speak in defense of the dragonseed. He remarked&nbsp;
that Ser Addam and his brother Alyn were "true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:45.120
heirs" and worthy of Driftmark and that Nettles&nbsp;
had fought valiantly in the Battle in the Gullet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:50.400
The Hand's impassioned protests were in vain as&nbsp;
by this time the queen had been betrayed so often,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:55.920
by so many, that she was quick to believe the&nbsp;
worst of any man. Queen Rhaenyra commanded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.920 --> 00:11:01.920
Ser Luthor Largent to arrest Addam in the&nbsp;
Dragonpit. Addam, who had been forewarned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.000
managed to make his escape&nbsp;
by flying away with Seasmoke.&nbsp;

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:09.600
When the balked and angry Luthor&nbsp;
returned from the Dragonpit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:16.400
he accused Corlys of treachery. Corlys did not&nbsp;
deny it. Bound and beaten, but still silent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:21.440
he was taken down into the Red Keep's dungeons&nbsp;
and thrown into a black cell to await trial and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:27.440
execution. This action lost Rhaenyra her fleet.
When it became known that Corlys had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:31.920
arrested, his men, who made up half of&nbsp;
Rhaenyra's forces at King's Landing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:37.040
began to abandon Rhaenyra by the hundreds.
This was the beginning of Rhaenyra's downfall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:41.600
which eventually cost her her life.
Once Aegon II Targaryen returned to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:46.880
King's Landing after feeding Rhaenyra to his&nbsp;
dragon, Lord Corlys was released and pardoned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:52.480
allowing him to serve Aegon on his small council.&nbsp;
Corlys did not simply betray the remaining members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:57.600
of the Blacks who were still in the field:
originally Aegon II considered executing Aegon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:04.080
III, who was (for all anyone knew) Rhaenyra's&nbsp;
last remaining child. But Aegon II needed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:09.280
wealth of House Velaryon and to ensure they&nbsp;
wouldn't continue fighting him, so in return,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:14.960
Corlys was able to negotiate the concessions&nbsp;
that he would have a seat on the small council,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:20.880
that Aegon III would be spared, and even that&nbsp;
Aegon III would be betrothed to Aegon II's last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:25.600
remaining child, Princess Jaehaera.
At one council meeting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:31.840
the Sea Snake openly called King Aegon II and his&nbsp;
small council "fools, liars, and oathbreakers"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:37.840
and stormed out. Lord Larys Strong afterwards&nbsp;
went to Corlys to bring him back on the council,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:43.600
and together they secretly plotted to end the war.
Following the defeat of Lord Borros Baratheon at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:48.320
the Battle of the Kingsroad, with an army of&nbsp;
rivermen near the city, and a second host, led&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:54.640
by Lord Cregan Stark, coming down the kingsroad,
Corlys advised Aegon II to join the Night's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.640 --> 00:13:00.640
Watch. The king refused but was mysteriously&nbsp;
poisoned soon after, thereby ending the war.&nbsp;

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:06.160
Following the death of Aegon II Targaryen, and&nbsp;
before the arrival of the Wolf of Winterfell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:10.320
who wanted to continue the war until all&nbsp;
late Rhaenyra's enemies were destroyed,&nbsp;

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:15.920
Corlys sent envoys to Casterly Rock,&nbsp;
Storm's End and Oldtown, who had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:22.720
Aegon II's main supporters, suing for peace.
Lord Corlys was arrested by Lord Stark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:28.640
in what became known as the Hour of the Wolf. He&nbsp;
was later freed thanks to an edict of King Aegon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:34.640
III Targaryen that Baela and Rhaena Targaryen&nbsp;
persuaded him to issue. Black Aly Blackwood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:41.200
agreed to marry Lord Stark if he honored the&nbsp;
edict, which he did. Thus Corlys was freed and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:47.280
served as one of the regents of young Aegon III.
Corlys was regarded as the most powerful of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:53.520
regents of the young king until his death of&nbsp;
old age in 132 AC, at the age of seventy-nine.&nbsp;

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:59.440
To honor him and all his deeds, his body was&nbsp;
placed beneath the Iron Throne for a week.&nbsp;

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:04.800
Corlys was then carried back to Driftmark where&nbsp;
the battered hull of his ancient ship Sea Snake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:10.160
was then floated one last time and towed out&nbsp;
into the deep waters with Corlys aboard it.&nbsp;

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:16.160
It was said afterward that as the hull went&nbsp;
down, the wild dragon Cannibal swept overhead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:21.760
his great black wings spread in a last salute.
Its only fitting to end this video about the Sea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:26.720
Snake with briliant writing of Gyldayn in&nbsp;
Fire And Blood, who writes this about him:&nbsp;

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:32.160
''Seventy-nine years of age, he had served four&nbsp;
kings and a queen sailed to the ends of the earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:38.240
raised House Velaryon to unprecedented levels of&nbsp;
wealth and power, married a princess who might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:43.840
have been a queen, fathered dragonriders,&nbsp;
built towns and fleets, proved his valor in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:50.000
times of war and his wisdom in times of peace. The&nbsp;
Seven Kingdoms would never see his like again.''&nbsp;

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:54.480
Let me know your thoughts about everything: the&nbsp;
prequel, its characters, especially the Sea Snake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:58.320
in the comment section down below. Thank you&nbsp;
